course: dictionary
lesson: 6889
title: Stretching a word too far
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word overstretch is built from over, which means too much, and stretch, which means to pull something longer or wider. To overstretch something is to stretch it too far.
explain: With a muscle, that means it gets hurt. «A strain is a muscle injury: some muscle fibres are overstretched, often when you sprint before warming up.» Warming up first helps protect your muscles.
explain: Overstretch can also describe people, money or services that are asked to do more than they can manage. Look at the clues around the word to tell which meaning the writer means.
fact: Over means too much, so overstretch means to stretch something too far.
fact: «Overstretched» can describe a muscle that has been pulled too far and hurt.
fact: «Most strains heal in one to three weeks.» Rest the muscle first, then move it gently, and do not stretch it hard.
fact: To overstretch yourself, a budget or people means to ask them to do more than they can manage.
exercise: «Some muscle fibres are overstretched, often when you sprint before warming up.» What does overstretched mean here? | Stretched in a warm bath | *Stretched too far and hurt | Shortened and made stronger | Stretched and then rested
exercise: What does the over in overstretch tell you? | *Too much | Very quickly | Again | Under, or not enough
exercise: A teacher says, «Our school is overstretched, with 40 children in every class.» What does overstretched mean here? | *Asked to do more than it can manage | Closed for the summer | Given extra money for new classrooms | Painted in bright colours
test: Which advice is best for a strain? | Stretch it as far as it will go every day | Run on it straight away | Wrap it in cling film and leave it for a year | *Rest it first, then move it gently and do not stretch it hard
test: «Most strains heal in one to three weeks.» How long can a strain take to heal? | *One to three weeks | One to three hours | It never heals | Six months
exam: Which sentence uses overstretch to mean asked to do more than can be managed? | The bridge was overstretched by the heavy lorry | The rubber band was stretched and then let go | The muscle was overstretched after the sprint | *The nurses were overstretched during the busy winter, with more patients than beds
